     "type": "NUMERICAL",
     "marks": 15.0,
     "text": "The following information relates to Thornbury International (TL).\n\nInformation:\n  Thornbury International (TL) has a total income for tax year 2026 of Rs. 3,500,000. Income is charged to tax at 5% on the first Rs. 400,000, at 10% on the portion above Rs. 400,000 up to Rs. 800,000, and at 20% on any portion above Rs. 800,000. No credit, rebate or relief is available.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  Where income spans bands, each band is charged separately: tax = (sum over bands of the portion of income in that band x the rate for that band). The whole of the income is NOT charged at the highest rate reached.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the tax liability band by band and the total tax payable for tax year 2026. Show all workings and state the effective rate on the total income. (15 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
