     "type": "SCENARIO",
     "marks": 11.0,
     "text": "Thornbury International (TL) has income and transactions during tax year 2026 in respect of which you are asked to advise.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Thornbury International (TL) has been assessed for tax year 2026 on an income of Rs. 120,000. It disputes the assessment and has sought to be informed of the grounds on which it was made.\n(b) Thornbury International (TL) was incorporated in Pakistan on 25 March 2026 and carries on a trading business. During tax year 2026 it earned income of Rs. 650,000 and paid a tax credit of Rs. 575,000.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Appeals, namely:\n(i) Most appeals arise on account of disagreement between the taxpayer and the tax collectors (income tax department) regarding the quantification of the taxable income and tax liability thereon as well as levy of default surcharge, penalties, etc.\n(ii) The taxpayer right of appeal. Usually an agreement is reached through correspondence or discussion and in most cases disputes are settled with the taxpayers at the Taxation Officer’s / Commissioner’s level, saving time and trouble all around.\n(iii) Following forums of appeal are available to an aggrieved person: Commissioner (Appeals) Appellate Tribunal High Court Supreme Court of Pakistan (against decision of reference to High Court).\n\nRequired:\nExplain what Thornbury International (TL) is required to do in respect of each of the matters described, stating the basis of each requirement. (11 marks)",
