     "marks": 15.0,
     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Enterprises (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  Coppervale Enterprises (CL) has taxable income of Rs. 2,090,000 for tax year 2026. The whole of this income falls within the slab above Rs. 3,000,000, which is charged at 5%. The company has no tax credits and no previous year losses.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  Tax on a slice of income = Slice x Rate applicable to that slice. Where income falls wholly within one slab, the whole amount is charged at that slab's rate.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the tax liability for tax year 2026, showing the rate applied and the workings. State the due date for payment. (15 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
