     "section": "B",
     "type": "NUMERICAL",
     "marks": 10.0,
     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Enterprises (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  Coppervale Enterprises (CL) agreed to pay Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) a fee of Rs. 3,975 net of tax. The fee is subject to withholding at 25%, which is to be deducted from the fee, so that Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) receives the stated net amount.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  Where an amount is stated net of a deduction, the gross amount is found by grossing up: Gross = Net / (1 - Deduction rate). The deduction is then Gross less Net.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the gross fee payable by Coppervale Enterprises (CL), the amount of tax to be deducted, and the net amount to be remitted to Quarrystone Enterprises (QL). Show all workings. (10 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
