     "type": "SCENARIO",
     "marks": 8.0,
     "text": "Coppervale Enterprises (CL) has income and transactions during tax year 2026 in respect of which you are asked to advise.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Coppervale Enterprises (CL) exports goods to Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) and received the export proceeds of Rs. 620,000 during tax year 2026. The goods left Pakistan on 17 October 2026.\n(b) Coppervale Enterprises (CL) carries on business in a province in which a provincial sales tax is levied, and made supplies of Rs. 700,000 during tax year 2026. It has not been registered for the tax.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Scope of Tax, namely:\n(i) Income tax law deals with the levy of tax on the income of a person.\n(ii) Applicable tax rates” Perusal of the aforesaid provision of law raises following questions in our minds: What is a tax year? ii. What is taxable income and how it is computed? iii. Who is person? iv. What are applicable rates of tax?\n(iii) These primary questions are answered in the upcoming paragraphs.\n\nRequired:\nExplain, with reference to the facts stated, the requirements engaged and the treatment required. Where a requirement is not engaged, say so. (8 marks)",
