     "text": "Thornbury Engineering (TL) operates a manufacturing and trading business and the cost and management information below relates to its operations.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Thornbury Engineering (TL) loads sales data to its reporting warehouse from 23 source systems. The extract that failed on 16 April 2026 was reported as a nil return and the figures were used in a board paper.\n(b) For a market study Thornbury Engineering (TL) used both its own sales records and published figures obtained from Glenmara Engineering (GL). It has documented neither source.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Characteristics of Big Data, namely:\n(i) The amount of data being generated is enormous and continuously growing. Organizations must process terabytes or even petabytes of data in real-time or near-real-time. The amount of data generated daily is staggering and continues to grow exponentially.\n(ii) Various sources like social media platforms, websites, IoT devices, sensors, transactions, videos, emails, and many other forms of digital communication.\n(iii) Importance of Big Data technologies to store, process, and analyze this vast influx of information.\n\nRequired:\nExplain, with reference to the facts stated, the requirements engaged and the treatment required. Where a requirement is not engaged, say so. (18 marks)",
