     "marks": 10.0,
     "text": "Explain the meaning of Compensation for Loss or Damage Caused by Breach as it applies in this subject, and state the requirements that follow from it.\n\nBreach of contract occurs when a party either refuses or fails to perform his part of contract other than when such performance is excused under the law.\nWhen a contract has been broken, the party who suffers by such breach is entitled to receive, from the party who has broken the contract, compensation for any loss or damage caused to him thereby, which naturally arose in the usual course of things from such...\nPrice and market price at the date of breach.  Example 01: Naveed promised to deliver food at an event organised by Adeel for 80 persons for Rs. 85,000. Just an hour before the event, Naveed informed that he would not be able to deliver the food.\n\nRequired:\nState the requirement and explain its purpose. (10 marks)",
