     "text": "The following facts relate to a transaction to which Coppervale Enterprises (CL) is a party. Advise Coppervale Enterprises (CL) on the position under the law applicable in Pakistan.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Coppervale Enterprises (CL) and Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) entered into a partnership on 7 December 2026 without registering the firm, and the business was carried on under the name of Coppervale Enterprises (CL).\n(b) Coppervale Enterprises (CL) took goods on hire from Quarrystone Enterprises (QL) on 7 December 2026 and sold them without the consent of Quarrystone Enterprises (QL).\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing The Features of a Company, namely:\n(i) A sole trader is an individual who owns and runs his or her own business. The law does not recognize the business: the law recognizes only the individual who runs it.\n(ii) A partnership is a group of individuals who own and run their own business. Each partner usually contributes capital to the business. A partnership business is not recognised as a ‘person’ by the law.\n(iii) Unlike sole traders and Partnerships, a company is a legal person, separate from its owners. This is called doctrine of corporate personality i.e.\n\nRequired:\nExplain, with reference to the facts stated, the requirements engaged and the treatment required. Where a requirement is not engaged, say so. (10 marks)",
