     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Productions (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  Coppervale Productions (CL) sells a single product at Rs. 400 per unit. The variable cost per unit is Rs. 350 and fixed costs for the year are Rs. 425,000. The company has no variable selling or distribution costs. Actual production and sales during the year were 20,000 units.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  Contribution per unit = Selling price per unit - Variable cost per unit. Break-even point in units = Fixed costs / Contribution per unit.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the contribution per unit, the break-even point in units and in Rupees, and the total contribution earned on actual sales. Show all workings and state the margin of safety in units. (15 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
