     "text": "The following information relates to Coppervale Productions (CL).\n\nInformation:\n  Coppervale Productions (CL) produced 2,400 units during the year and sold 1,900 units. There was no opening or closing work in progress and no opening inventory. The variable production cost per unit is Rs. 100 and production overheads of Rs. 45 per unit are fixed in total for the period. Selling and distribution costs are Rs. 120,000 in total, fixed in the period.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  Under absorption costing, production overheads are absorbed into inventory at a fixed rate per unit. Under marginal costing, fixed production overheads are charged in full to the period. The difference in profit is the overhead absorbed into closing inventory, or the overhead released from opening inventory.\n\nRequired:\nCalculate the closing inventory under each method, the profit under marginal costing and under absorption costing, and explain why the two profits differ. Show all workings. (8 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
