     "type": "NUMERICAL",
     "marks": 10.0,
     "text": "The following information relates to Thornbury Limited (TL).\n\nInformation:\n  Thornbury Limited (TL) purchased inventory of US$ 59,000 on 13 May 2026 when the exchange rate was US$ 1 = Rs. 196. The inventory was still held at the reporting date, when the rate was US$ 1 = Rs. 206. No exchange difference has been recognised in relation to this balance to date.\n\nYou are given the following relationship:\n  A monetary item denominated in a foreign currency is translated at the rate at the reporting date. A non-monetary item measured at historical cost continues to be translated at the rate at the date of the transaction.\n\nRequired:\nState the rate at which this balance is translated at the reporting date and calculate the amount in Rupees, together with the exchange difference arising since acquisition and where it is recognised. Show all workings. (10 marks)\n\nNote to candidates: the relationship stated above is given. Marks are not awarded for reproducing it. You are required to show all workings and to state any assumption on which your answer depends.",
