     "text": "You are engaged to advise Coppervale Corporation (CL) on the corporate and reporting matters described below.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Coppervale Corporation (CL) acquired 60% of the share capital of Quarrystone Corporation (QL) on 16 December 2026 for Rs. 720,000. Quarrystone Corporation (QL) is not a subsidiary of any other company.\n(b) Coppervale Corporation (CL) disposed of 21 per cent of its holding in Quarrystone Corporation (QL) on 16 December 2026, retaining 21 per cent. The disposal reduced its voting rights from control to significant influence.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Single Economic Entity Concept and Control, namely:\n(i) Many large businesses actually consist of several separate legal entities controlled by one central company i.e. parent or holding entity. The entities controlled by parent entity are called subsidiaries.\n(ii) Entity as well as the subsidiary companies to get the idea about the financial health of the entire (large) business. Therefore, the parent entities are required to present their individual financial statements and also the consolidated financial statements...\n(iii) Consolidated financial statements helpful in understanding the overall financial position and financial performance of the entire entity i.e. group.\n\nRequired:\nDiscuss the requirements that arise on the facts given, and advise Coppervale Corporation (CL) on the treatment to be adopted in respect of each. (10 marks)",
