     "text": "The board of Coppervale Consulting (CL) is considering the matters described below and requires your advice before taking a decision.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Coppervale Consulting (CL) has prepared a budget for the coming year on the basis of last year's costs adjusted for inflation. The production manager was not consulted before it was circulated, and the sales target is unchanged from the previous year.\n(b) Coppervale Consulting (CL) has reviewed its own resources and competences and concluded that the distribution network it built at a cost of Rs. 290,000 cannot be replicated by competitors, while its purchasing arrangements can be matched by any of them within a year.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Basics of Budgeting, namely:\n(i) A budget is a quantitative estimation of costs, revenues and resources of an entity for a defined period of time. Budgeting has always been part of the activities of any business organization as it helps the business in better understanding of its business...\n(ii) Resources will be required. This helps the management to have a better understanding of resources to be arranged and managed, resulting in a smooth flow of operations and avoiding unfavourable surprises.\n(iii) Budgeting and Forecasting are two important constituents of managerial decision-making process. To avoid crises in the business, managers and owners make use of two essential tools – forecasting and budgeting.\n\nRequired:\nSet out, with reasons, the treatment required for each of the matters described, and the disclosures that must accompany them. (15 marks)",
