     "type": "SCENARIO",
     "marks": 11.0,
     "text": "Your firm is the external auditor of Thornbury Limited (TL), a listed company. The following matters came to your attention during the audit.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) After the reporting date, Glenmara Limited (GL) issued a formal claim against Thornbury Limited (TL) for Rs. 170,000.\n(b) Thornbury Limited (TL) asked Glenmara Limited (GL) to act as its auditor, and named a person as the proposed engagement partner who has audited another company in the same group. No suitability assessment of the proposed partner's independence was carried out.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing The Role of Substantive Procedures, namely:\n(i) The following chapters describe a variety of substantive procedures that an auditor might carry out. In your exam, you might be asked to suggest what substantive procedures ought to be carried out in a particular situation.\n(ii) Appropriate in one situation would be inappropriate in another. What you need to be able to do in the examination is apply general principles of substantive testing to the particular system or business described in the question.\n(iii) What am I being asked to test? Start by asking what it is that you should be trying to test, and obtain evidence about.\n\nRequired:\nExplain, with reference to the facts stated, the requirements engaged and the treatment required. Where a requirement is not engaged, say so. (11 marks)",
