     "text": "Your firm is the external auditor of Coppervale Corporation (CL), a listed company. The following matters came to your attention during the audit.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Coppervale Corporation (CL) is a charitable organisation funded by donations. The audit team was unable to obtain confirmation of contributions recorded in the year of Rs. 290,000, and the organisation's governing document restricts the use of its funds to purposes not stated in the accounts.\n(b) Coppervale Corporation (CL) changed its depreciation method on 28 February 2026 without restating comparatives and without disclosure.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing The Meaning of Audit, namely:\n(i) An audit is an official examination of the accounts (or accounting systems) of an entity (by an auditor). When an auditor examines the accounts of an entity, what is he looking for?\n(ii) Statements of an entity are prepared according to an applicable financial reporting framework. Financial statements –A structured representation of historical financial information, including disclosures, intended to communicate an entity’s economic resources...\n(iii) Applicable financial reporting framework – The financial reporting framework adopted by management and, where appropriate, those charged with governance in the preparation of the financial statements that is acceptable in view of the nature of the entity and...\n\nRequired:\nFor each of the matters described, state the requirement that applies and the treatment that follows, giving reasons in each case. (12 marks)",
