     "text": "Your firm is the external auditor of Coppervale Corporation (CL), a listed company. The following matters came to your attention during the audit.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) No physical inventory count was held at the reporting date. Management has estimated closing inventory at Rs. 100,000.\n(b) Inventory of Rs. 510,000 was held at a location that was not visited by the audit team. Management requested a visit after the reporting date.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Audit Evidence: ISA 500, namely:\n(i) To be able to draw reasonable conclusions on which to base his audit opinion.\n(ii) Procedures for the purpose of obtaining sufficient, appropriate audit evidence.\n(iii) Consider the relevance and reliability of the information to be used as audit evidence.\n\nRequired:\nSet out the requirements relevant to the matters above and the treatment that each requires, together with any disclosure the requirements oblige. (10 marks)",
