     "text": "You are the audit manager responsible for the audit of Coppervale Corporation (CL) for the year ended 30 June 2026. The matters below have arisen during the audit.\n\nThe following facts have been established:\n(a) Coppervale Corporation (CL) receives a significant part of its income from Quarrystone Corporation (QL), a company controlled by a director. The transactions in the year were of Rs. 260,000 and were not disclosed.\n(b) A loan of Rs. 160,000 was advanced to a director on 5 November 2026 on terms no less favourable than those available to third parties.\n\nThe requirements to be considered in answering this question are those governing Related Parties: ISA 550, namely:\n(i) Enron used special purpose entities-limited partnerships or companies, created to fulfil a temporary or specific purpose, to fund or manage risks associated with specific assets.\n(ii) Its debt. Why the International Auditing and Assurance Standards Board require the auditor to obtain sufficient appropriate audit evidence regarding related parties?\n(iii) “The objective of this Standard is to ensure that an entity’s financial statements contain the disclosures necessary to draw attention to the possibility that its financial position and profit or loss may have been affected by the existence of related parties...\n\nRequired:\nExplain, with reference to the facts stated, the requirements engaged and the treatment required. Where a requirement is not engaged, say so. (10 marks)",
